{"page": 20, "text": "In the first quarter of 2026, we issued an additional aggregate $150 million of the Notes due March 2029 with identical terms to the prior notes outstanding. In the second quarter of 2026, we borrowed an additional $150 million under the Term Loan due March 2028 and extended the maturity date to May 2031. The proceeds of the additional term loan borrowing were used to repay the Notes due March 2027. In the third quarter of 2026, we completed a tender offer and redeemed an aggregate $46 million of the Notes due January 2037 and Notes due March 2043 and recorded a gain of $5 million in other (income) expense. Also, in the third quarter of 2026, we amended the Term loan due March 2032 to reduce the spread by 0.75%. We maintain a $450 million revolving credit facility (increased from $400 million in the first quarter of 2026) that matures in May 2031. This credit facility requires that we maintain (with maintenance tested quarterly) (i) a Consolidated Interest Coverage Ratio (as defined in the credit facility agreement) of not less than 2.00 to 1.00, (ii) a Consolidated Secured Net Leverage Ratio (as defined in the credit facility agreement) of no greater than 3.00 to 1.00 and (iii) a Consolidated Total Net Leverage Ratio (as defined in the credit facility agreement) of no greater than (a) 4.75 to 1.00 for each of the fiscal quarters in 2026, (b) 4.50 to 1.00 for each of the fiscal quarters in 2027, (c) 4.25 to 1.00 for each of the fiscal quarters in 2028 and (d) 4.00 to 1.00 for each fiscal quarter thereafter. At September 30, 2026, we were in compliance with these financial covenants. During 2026, we borrowed an aggregate $177 million under this credit facility, $80 million of which was borrowed in the third quarter, and was fully repaid by September 30, 2026. At September 30, 2026, we have remaining borrowing capacity of $427 million. Borrowings under this credit facility are secured by assets of the Company. The credit facility also contains pr